Found while implementing #9 (git_index_find_prefix), whose POD sits right
below this one. Left alone there to keep that change surgical.

lib/Git/Libgit2/FFI.pm, =func git_index_find:

    Find the position of an entry by path. Returns C<UINT_MAX> if not found.

Two things wrong with that sentence:

1. git_index_find returns an int error code, not a position. On a miss it
   returns GIT_ENOTFOUND (-3), verified against libgit2 1.5.1:

       find "tasks/" rc=-3     # no such path in the index

   UINT_MAX never appears anywhere in the return.

2. It says nothing about the out-param, which is where the position
   actually lands, and nothing about the fact that libgit2 leaves that
   out-param untouched on a miss -- so an unset `my $pos` comes back as 0,
   a perfectly valid position. Same trap as documented for
   git_index_find_prefix in #9; the sibling entry should say it too.

The header docs for both, for reference:

    @param at_pos the address to which the position of the index entry is written (optional)
    @return 0 or an error code

Fix: rewrite the sentence in the style now used by git_index_find_prefix
directly below it -- return code, out-param meaning, and the "only trust
the position when the return is 0" caveat. Also note at_pos is optional
(undef passes a NULL through, empirically confirmed for this signature
shape).
Fixed in the working tree (uncommitted).

lib/Git/Libgit2/FFI.pm, =func git_index_find: the UINT_MAX sentence is gone.
Rewritten in the shape of the git_index_find_prefix entry directly below --
returns 0 on a hit and GIT_ENOTFOUND on a miss, the return value is an error
code and never a position, the position lands in the out-param, the
out-param is only meaningful when the return is 0 (libgit2 leaves it alone
on a miss, so an unset my $pos comes back as 0), at_pos is optional and
undef passes NULL through. Closes with a pointer to git_index_find_prefix
for the directory question.

Both new claims are now pinned by tests in t/20-index.t under #10:
GIT_ENOTFOUND on a miss, the out-param left at 0 on a miss, and the
undef/NULL at_pos call. Mutating the GIT_ENOTFOUND expectation to 0 makes
the suite red (GOT -3, CHECK 0).

podchecker on FFI.pm reports only the pre-existing PodWeaver directives
